      "side": 1,
      "message": "Any specific reason why we moved from the earlier state machine implementation to this kind of an implementation? I thought the earlier implementation had more flexibilities (although not needed currently) of having cleaner implementations on receiving the same event type in different states; for example on reception of EAP_START, if we had to do something different in AUTHORIZED or UNAUTHORIZED state before transistioning to the STARTED state.",
