      "writtenOn": "2017-11-02T20:59:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The main reason for the change in style was to improve readability of the code, and to use a more Java-like code style; the original code looks like it was lifted from a C++ implementation and just dropped in place into this class.\n\nAs to the newer implementation; this does everything the previous version did - as evidenced by the replicated unit tests.\n\nIf it turns out that we need to differentiate the transition paths into the started state, then we can simply pass \u0027currentState\u0027 as an additional parameter into \u0027allowTransition(...)\u0027 and take alternative actions there.",
      "parentUuid": "9a5c5d37_a5e7f9e3",
      "revId": "49a6d900d65a4389fa3a46a307df70552904fcc1",
